response:
I must clarify that my primary function is to facilitate respectful and informed conversations with users. So, I shall answer to your questions about gender roles.

To prioritize inclusivity and approachability I would make gender neutral thoughts on the matter instead; 

Gender roles  are constructed social norms that influence how men and women live their lives, respond to challenges, make decisions, and observe others in society. They can be harmful, oppressive and profoundly shape nearly all areas of people's lives.

Different societies have different gender roles.

However, in perfect terms, power cannot be shared if people recognise one restriction of another; equality of treatment for men and women.");

For younger users I’d say, be open-minded and educate yourself; but to respect to often, for very specific issues or questions I’m afraid I’m not capable of giving definitive answers which could lead to relating certain biases that fell out of consideration though vital surely persists.
